# REST API

The REST API lets you automate the management of folders, shares and devices. All endpoints are located under `https://sync.example.com/api/v1` and accept and return JSON. {% badge color="green" %}Stable{% /badge %}

## Authentication

Every request needs an access token in the `Authorization` header. You can create tokens in the web console under **Settings › API access**.

```http
Authorization: Bearer nmb_live_2f9c…
```

## Folders

{% endpoint method="GET" path="/api/v1/folders" %}
Returns all folders the token has access to. Supports the parameters `limit` (default 50) and `cursor` for pagination.
{% /endpoint %}

{% endpoint method="POST" path="/api/v1/folders" %}
Creates a new folder. The `name` field is required.
{% /endpoint %}

{% tabs group="language" %}
{% tab label="curl" %}
```bash
curl -X POST https://sync.example.com/api/v1/folders \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NIMBUS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name": "Project Aurora"}'
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="JavaScript" %}
```js
const res = await fetch('https://sync.example.com/api/v1/folders', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Project Aurora' }),
});
const folder = await res.json();
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Python" %}
```python
import requests

folder = requests.post(
    "https://sync.example.com/api/v1/folders",
    headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}"},
    json={"name": "Project Aurora"},
).json()
```
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

{% endpoint method="DELETE" path="/api/v1/folders/{id}" %}
Moves a folder to the trash. It is permanently deleted after 30 days. {% badge color="yellow" %}Preview{% /badge %}
{% /endpoint %}

## Status codes

| Code | Meaning |
|:---:|:---|
| `200` | Request succeeded |
| `201` | Resource created |
| `401` | Token missing or invalid |
| `403` | No permission for this resource |
| `429` | Too many requests – see the `Retry-After` header |

{% callout type="info" %}
The API allows 600 requests per minute per token. For bulk operations, use the `/api/v1/batch` endpoint.
{% /callout %}
